## Purpose

This license lets you use, modify, and share this software for free if you are
below the size thresholds in **Free Use**, or if one of the **Always-Free Uses**
applies to you. Organizations above those thresholds need a commercial license.

Every released version of the software converts to the Apache License, Version
2.0 two years after that version was first published, so nothing licensed under
these terms stays restricted permanently.

## Acceptance

To receive this license, you must agree to its rules. The rules of this license
are both obligations under your agreement with the licensor and conditions to
your license. You must not do anything under this license that breaks any of its
rules.

## Free Use

You may use the software free of charge if, at all times while you use it, **all
three** of the following are true of you and your affiliates taken together:

1. fewer than 10 individuals work for you, counting employees, officers, and
   individual contractors;

2. your revenue in your most recently completed fiscal year was less than
   US $1,000,000; and

3. the total external investment you have ever received is less than
   US $1,000,000, counted cumulatively across all rounds and instruments.

These figures are fixed. They are not indexed to inflation and do not change
over time. If you exceed any one of the three, Free Use ends and you need a
commercial license, unless an Always-Free Use applies to you.

## Always-Free Uses

Whether or not you meet the thresholds above, this license is free for:

1. **Individuals**, for personal, hobby, learning, or portfolio use.

2. **Nonprofit organizations, educational institutions, government bodies, and
   public research organizations**, for their own activities.

3. **Evaluation** by any organization, for up to 30 consecutive days, to decide
   whether to obtain a commercial license.

